A||||10||BN Boomer||At last! Pics of my 85 GT!||||10||
Z||000000||BN Boomer||07-08-2000||11:27 AM||||Phew, this thing is finally coming all together. I finished up the motor swap last week and got it back on the road, my radio arrived about the same time, the wiring harness adapter I had to order got here on Thursday, and my refinished door emblems from Oreif were waiting for me in the mail along with it. Yeah! <P>So, without further ado, here she is....<P>This is along the river near the switchyard where I work. Not too bad for $1200, eh? Even came with the extra motor to replace the tired stocker.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/85gt2.jpg"> <P>Here's an overall view of the interior. She's pretty clean for a 115,000 mile car. The fact that an older lady, an insurance agent even, was the previous owner might have a played a hand in that.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/85gt3.jpg"> <P>Here's a closer view of the AM/FM/CD player out of a 97 Sunfire that I picked up for $50. I had to order a wiring harness adapter from <A HREF="http://www.newellelectronics.com/" TARGET=_blank>Newell Electronics</A> to interface with the factory Fiero harness and avoid messy splicing. The guys at Newell are great. Not only did they have a great price on the adapter, but they helped me unlock the Theftlock code on my new radio. Simply awesome service. Two thumbs up from Boomer. I think this is actually a pretty nice radio. It doesn't seem to take much to fill a Fiero with sound, although a speaker upgrade is probably in the not-too-distant future.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/85gt1.jpg"> <P>And here's the door emblems Oreif did up for me, although I don't think this pic does them the justice they deserve. These things look GREAT! <B>BIG</B> thanks, Orief!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/85gt4.jpg"> <P>Overall, I really LOVE this car. It is in pretty good condition for it's age and mileage. I'm looking for some adhesive to fix up the delaminating interior consoles right now. The suspension is definitely going to be getting a going over, too. I'm planning on new shocks, struts, tie rod ends, polyurethane bushings all the way around, maybe doing the Cadillac ball joint thing ala batboy, and using the old front swaybar from my parts car in the rear of this one. Grand Am front brakes along with new wheel bearings are also not too far in the future. I am also already thinking about some sort of engine upgrade. I'm not sure if I want to build the original 2.8 into a 3.1 or just cough up the money and go with a 3.4. I suspect the latter is what will happen once I sell my pickup and hopefully get some sort of bonus when, or if ever it sometimes seems, our union settles a new contract with the railroads. I guess only time will tell.<P>Anyhow, that's my story and I'm sticking to it. Thanks for looking, folks!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||Oreif||07-08-2000||12:00 PM||||Boomer, Great looking car! Are the seats original? I thought only 84 had the fleece inserts but I could be wrong. Anyhow Very sharp car. Thanks for the link to Newell.<BR>I'm always looking for links to aid others.<BR>Glad you like the emblems!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||BN Boomer||07-08-2000||12:12 PM||||Oreif, I'm pretty sure this car is entirely stock (well, except for the radio now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). It seems like I've heard that the suede seats with the fleece inserts were only available in 84, too, but then I saw them in this 85. I seriously doubt that either of the two older women who previously owned this car would have swapped them around.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||07-08-2000||12:37 PM||||Boomer, GREAT looking car!!! you did good on the radio too!!! Glad you got a hold of Bobby Newell, he is wonderful to work with and deserves all the support we can give him on her, doncha think??? and, just so you know, if you ever decide to show it in a FOCOA event, registering in stock class they allow up to five changes and still be able to compete as stock so the radio thing is ok!!<P>Glad you are mobile now - it looks wonderful!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
